From 321e08799ee4dcdc28399a08605efaf10f1a8aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:48:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] CUDA/HIP: run consecutive matrix-vector products on the
 same vector in one mmvf launch

Up to four consecutive MUL_MAT nodes with the same F32 vector src1 and 2D
F32/F16/BF16 src0 of one type and row length run as one mul_mat_vec_f grid:
the rows of the grid go through the matrices in turn, each block writes to
its matrix's dst. Separate Q/K/V-style projections of one input stop paying a
launch each.

New test-backend-ops case MUL_MAT_SAME_SRC1 (F32/F16/BF16, 2 to 4 matrices,
row counts with and without a multiple of 256), all pass on ROCm with the
MUL_MAT tolerance; the unfused path has the same errors.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh   |  8 +++++
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu | 55 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvf.cu      | 38 +++++++++++++++++++---
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp      | 57 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 153 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

